<xsd:schema
    xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema"
    targetNamespace="a"
    xmlns:a="a"
    elementFormDefault="qualified">

    <xsd:element name="numericPattern" type="a:NumericPattern"/>

    <xsd:complexType name="NumericPattern">
        <xsd:sequence>
            <!--
              A numeric type must not carry a pattern: no Bean Validation constraint can honor it.

              Two reasons, and this fixture is written so that both stay visible:
               - @Pattern resolves to the Pattern validator, which accepts CharSequence only, so
                 it cannot validate a number at all - it fails at validation time instead of
                 checking anything;
               - a pattern is not a numeric range: "[0-9]3[0-9]*" pins the digit 3 in second
                 position, which no minInclusive/maxInclusive pair can express.

              The pattern below is deliberately of the second kind. A literal value would hide
              the limit, because it happens to be expressible as a range; this one shows why
              "just translate the pattern into numeric facets" is not a general answer.

              So no pattern validation may be imported for these fields - scalar or collection.
              To constrain a numeric value, use numeric facets (minInclusive + maxInclusive).

              The same simpleType is used twice, once scalar and once as a collection, so this
              fixture is the verification gate for anyone adding pattern support to numbers.
            -->
            <xsd:element name="patternedInteger" type="a:PatternedInteger"
                         minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1"/>
            <xsd:element name="patternedIntegerList" type="a:PatternedInteger"
                         minOccurs="2" maxOccurs="4"/>
        </xsd:sequence>
    </xsd:complexType>

    <xsd:simpleType name="PatternedInteger">
        <xsd:restriction base="xsd:integer">
            <xsd:pattern value="[0-9]3[0-9]*"/>
        </xsd:restriction>
    </xsd:simpleType>

</xsd:schema>
